# Headless CMS monorepo

## Layout

| Directory | Stack | Cursor rules |
|-----------|-------|----------------|
| `next-headless-cms-fe/` | Next.js multi-tenant CMS | **`.cursor/rules/`** — use these for all frontend work |
| `headless-cms-backend/` | Strapi v5 | **`headless-cms-backend/.cursor/rules/`** — start with `strapi-backend.mdc` |

## Where to look

- **Human docs**: repo root `README.md`; frontend `next-headless-cms-fe/docs/` (`DEVELOPMENT.md`, `BUILD-VERIFICATION.md`)
- **Frontend architecture, blocks, deploy, i18n**: `next-headless-cms-fe/.cursor/rules/`
- **Frontend agents**: `next-headless-cms-fe/.cursor/rules/rules-sync.mdc`
- **Backend / Strapi CMS model & API**: `headless-cms-backend/.cursor/rules/` (`content-model.mdc`, `api-contract.mdc`)
- **Per tenant (frontend)**: `next-headless-cms-fe/.cursor/rules/tenants/{tenant-id}/catalog.mdc`

## GitHub Actions

Workflows are at repo root: `.github/workflows/`. They set `working-directory: next-headless-cms-fe` for frontend jobs.

## When editing backend

Strapi schemas and seed data live in `headless-cms-backend/`. Target types: **`page`**, **`navigation`** (see `content-model.mdc`). Frontend still uses `dataAdapter: "mock"` until migration.

When the REST contract changes, update backend rules + `strapi.adapter.ts` + frontend types in one change set (`headless-cms-backend/.cursor/rules/rules-sync.mdc`).
